BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OpenLAB 2026 | Horrores encriptados: los Lost Media en el folclore
  digital – Conferencia de Arianna Caserta — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261127T000000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261127T000000
DTSTAMP:20261128T075510Z
UID:9d5d1e7706b1907bf32f2bfc1c1f@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:En un mundo hipervisual donde casi nada escapa al panóptico d
 igital\, los lost media son artefactos paradójicos: fragmentos de cultura
  mediática cuya existencia es objeto de rumores y de los que solo permane
 cen rastros parciales. Se buscan colectivamente en Reddit y YouTube\, a me
 dio camino entre el folclore en línea y la resistencia a la transparencia
  absoluta de las grandes plataformas. Así\, recuperan algo del «aura» d
 e los objetos de culto: importa más que existan que llegar a verlos. Como
  las creepypastas\, su incompletitud y su ambigüedad estimulan la creaci
 ón colaborativa de mitos. Y acercan los lost media al terror. Del desktop
  cinema y el first-person shooter a la exploración de Google \nCategory: 
 Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/sch
 edule/openlab-festival-mechanics-truth
LOCATION:Nave Una\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/openlab-festival-mechanics-
 truth
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OpenLAB 2026 | Visual Trust. A Multi-modal and Experimental Projec
 t – Presentation by Amanda Bernal Pérez — Madrid
DTSTART;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261127T000000
DTEND;TZID="UTC+01:00":20261127T000000
DTSTAMP:20261128T075510Z
UID:f4e4d2b6596ed0172ec76b713a72@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:What makes people from different cultures and societies trust 
 (or distrust) an image? How is the visual fake assessed and debunked in sc
 ience\, religion\, AI or documentary photography? What is the relation bet
 ween image-making and visual trust? Amanda Bernal introduces Visual Trust
 \, an experimental and multimodal research initiative funded by the Europe
 an Research Council (2021-2027). Drawing mainly on anthropology\, the proj
 ect takes a comparative approach to current regimes of visual authenticity
  and forgery. Bernal presents the main guidelines and methods of the proje
 ct through some of its outcomes: films\, photo-essays and texts. This acti
 vity is part of the OpenLAB The Mechanics of Truth f\nCategory: Multidisci
 plinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/open
 lab-2026-visual-trust-multi-modal-and-experimental-project-presentation-am
 anda-bernal
LOCATION:Nave 17. Aulario\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.mataderomadrid.org/en/schedule/openlab-2026-visual-trust-m
 ulti-modal-and-experimental-project-presentation-amanda-bernal
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:europe
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:matadero-madrid
END:VEVENT
